examples.question_text:
The rectangles are similar. The smaller rectangle has area $18\text{ cm}^2$. Find the area of the larger rectangle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (2,1);
\draw (3.4,0) rectangle (6.4,1.5);
\path (1,1) node[above] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\path (1,0.5) node {$18\text{ cm}^2$};
\path (4.9,1.5) node[above] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
